---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';import {repo} from '../lib/apps';
---
<Layout title="Submit an App" description="Contribute a complete BUSY Bar app through a GitHub pull request."><article class="prose-page"><span class="eyebrow">Add to the Workbench</span><h1>Submit an App</h1><p>Share a complete app that someone else can download and run. Contributions arrive as pull requests in this site’s GitHub repository.</p><h2>Prepare Your App</h2><ol><li>Fork the repository and create a folder under <code>apps/tedt/your-app-slug/</code>.</li><li>Include <code>app.py</code>, a <code>manifest.yaml</code>, a PNG, GIF, JPEG, or WebP preview, and an MIT <code>LICENSE</code>.</li><li>Include every supporting module, asset, configuration example, and a <code>requirements.txt</code> when needed. Never include credentials or personal configuration.</li><li>Add a <code>README.md</code> explaining what the app does, how to configure it, and how to run it.</li><li>Run <code>npm ci</code>, <code>npm test</code>, and <code>npm run build</code>, then open a pull request.</li></ol><p><a class="button primary" href={`${repo}/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md`}>Read the Contribution Guide</a> <a class="button secondary" href={`${repo}/fork`}>Fork the Repository</a></p><h2>Have an Idea Instead?</h2><p>You do not need working code to start a conversation. <a href="/ideas/">Record an app idea</a> and describe the problem it would solve.</p><h2>About the Community Mirror</h2><p>Apps from <a href="https://maxswinkels.github.io/busybar-apps/">Max Swinkels’s gallery</a> are imported automatically with their original attribution. Send changes to those apps to their original project or gallery. Local submissions are maintained independently here.</p></article></Layout>
